@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+BOUND SYMBOL
+LblapplyBin'LParUndsCommUndsCommUndsRParUnds'MPY-CORE'Unds'Val'Unds'String'Unds'Val'Unds'Val
+
+FROZEN OPERATIONAL INVENTORY
+COMMAND:
+  rg '^\s*rule applyBin' /reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/*.k | wc -l
+RESULT:
+  32
+
+CANDIDATE DEFINITION
+  | "+", Float left, Float right => Float (addF left right)
+  | "-", Float left, Float right => Float (Float.sub left right)
+  | _, _, _ => noneV
+
+The fallback contradicts ordinary frozen operational equations rather than
+merely totalizing K-stuck inputs.
+
+ADVERSARIAL WITNESS 1
+Input: applyBin("+", inj_Int(2), inj_Int(3))
+Frozen source: reference-semantics/semantics/int.k:9
+  rule applyBin("+", I1:Int, I2:Int) => I1 +Int I2
+Frozen result: inj_Int(5)
+Candidate result by definitional reduction: noneV
+
+ADVERSARIAL WITNESS 2
+Input: applyBin("*", inj_Float(2.0), inj_Float(3.0))
+Frozen source: reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:115-117
+  syntax Float ::= mulF(Float, Float) [...]
+  rule applyBin("*", F1:Float, F2:Float) => mulF(F1, F2)
+Frozen result: inj_Float(mulF(2.0, 3.0))
+Candidate result by definitional reduction: noneV
+
+A Lean witness file was placed at
+/tmp/audit-work/lean-audit/OperationalWitness.lean with rfl statements for
+the two candidate fallback results.
+
+COMMAND
+  LAKE_HOME=/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0 \
+  LEAN_SYSROOT=/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0 \
+  lake env lean OperationalWitness.lean
+RESULT
+error: failed to locate application
+EXIT_CODE: 1
+
+COUNTERFACTUAL MUTATION
+A separate /tmp/audit-work/lean-audit/Counterfactual.lean changes both addF
+and subF to constant 0.0 and changes the two corresponding applyBin branches
+to return 0.0. It carries the same structural proof of the generated target,
+showing why operational interpretation must be audited independently.
+
+COMMAND
+  LAKE_HOME=/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0 \
+  LEAN_SYSROOT=/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0 \
+  lake env lean Counterfactual.lean
+RESULT
+error: failed to locate application
+EXIT_CODE: 1
+
+OTHER PARAMETER JUDGMENTS
+addF: Float.add matches +Float/addF on the bound float domain.
+subF: Float.sub matches -Float/subF on the bound float domain.
+isFloat: exact singleton-Float K-sequence predicate.
+project:Float?: exact optional projection on that same shape.
+projectFloat: identity on injected Float values; the 0.0 totalization is only
+outside the isFloat guard, where the frozen proof-local total helper has no
+value equation.
+
+FINAL OPERATIONAL-BRIDGE RESULT
+FAIL: the global applyBin definition is a hard-coded, semantically false
+totalization despite making the three generated equations easy to prove.

